{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01082",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.64,
      "end_seconds": 3.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Okay, morning, come on through."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.03,
      "end_seconds": 6.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "Hi there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.23,
      "end_seconds": 16.48,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Well, uh, hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.7,
      "end_seconds": 25.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.32,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 26.03,
      "end_seconds": 32.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "Doctor, it's an itchy rash all over. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.44,
      "end_seconds": 37.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Sure. Okay, is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.05,
      "end_seconds": 43.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Maybe a six out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.89,
      "end_seconds": 48.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.16,
      "end_seconds": 57.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Right, when it starts I tend to get a tingling mouth as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.82,
      "end_seconds": 63.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "What about swelling of your lips, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.11,
      "end_seconds": 94.15,
      "duration_seconds": 29.04,
      "text": "Yes, for two weeks. As for swelling of my lips, it happens on and off. As for tingling mouth, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. I did have hives at one point, uh, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.23,
      "end_seconds": 98.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Any fainting or wheeze?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.25,
      "end_seconds": 103.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.6,
      "end_seconds": 109.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "A few quick ones: throat tightness, new food or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.03,
      "end_seconds": 117.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.83,
      "end_seconds": 123.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.64,
      "end_seconds": 126.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.78,
      "end_seconds": 129.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.35,
      "end_seconds": 134.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Yeah, bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.06,
      "end_seconds": 143.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.9,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.64,
      "end_seconds": 156.13,
      "duration_seconds": 11.49,
      "text": "I take Seretide inhaler, twice a day. Sorry, uh, what was I saying, it's Thyronorm, every morning for my thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.28,
      "end_seconds": 159.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.11,
      "end_seconds": 167.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "It's 50 micrograms. Furosemide. I take it 40 milligrams, maybe, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.05,
      "end_seconds": 173.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Alright, do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.94,
      "end_seconds": 186.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.4,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, not with me. I'll bring it next time. Cetirizine. I take it 10 milligrams, when it flares."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.65,
      "end_seconds": 191.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.55,
      "end_seconds": 196.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Yeah, no, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.0,
      "end_seconds": 214.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.04,
      "end_seconds": 231.45,
      "duration_seconds": 16.41,
      "text": "Well, yes, asthma. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. An underactive thyroid, for about a year. Let me think, um, I've had heart failure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.83,
      "end_seconds": 244.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "Ah. Right, so an underactive thyroid is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.9,
      "end_seconds": 255.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.24,
      "end_seconds": 266.71,
      "duration_seconds": 10.47,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years. My partner and our baby. I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.2,
      "end_seconds": 274.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.11,
      "end_seconds": 280.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.36,
      "end_seconds": 285.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.1,
      "end_seconds": 299.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Right, that's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.54,
      "end_seconds": 320.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 66, temperature 37.0, blood pressure 111 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.54,
      "end_seconds": 325.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.95,
      "end_seconds": 327.65,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.27,
      "end_seconds": 332.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "So, tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.67,
      "end_seconds": 359.86,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "There are raised pink welts on the trunk and arms, the lips are a little puffy, and the tongue and throat look normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.38,
      "end_seconds": 362.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.83,
      "end_seconds": 367.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.05,
      "end_seconds": 402.9,
      "duration_seconds": 20.85,
      "text": "Putting it all together, this looks most like an allergic reaction, possibly to a recently started medicine. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. It could also be a viral rash, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.21,
      "end_seconds": 405.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.64,
      "end_seconds": 423.3,
      "duration_seconds": 15.66,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an allergic reaction, possibly to a recently started medicine. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had an itchy rash all over, and no vomiting or fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.74,
      "end_seconds": 426.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.06,
      "end_seconds": 457.46,
      "duration_seconds": 29.4,
      "text": "The treatment will be chlorphenamine, 4 milligrams, every six hours, for three days. You take it by mouth. That's for allergic rash. Stop the new tablet until we know what caused it and write down every medicine you took in the last week. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 459.09,
      "end_seconds": 462.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 463.4,
      "end_seconds": 480.1,
      "duration_seconds": 16.7,
      "text": "If your throat tightens, your lips swell further or you get breathless, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Let's review you in two days. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 480.98,
      "end_seconds": 484.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Well, thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}